close_reason: "Public URLs with an at sign in the path survive redaction, and identities can no longer store or echo URL credentials"
contract_change:
  api: "URL credential redaction in refusals and recoveries; author, assignee and claim identities"
  before: "A public URL with an @ in its path lost its host and path and withheld the retry; a credential-bearing PM_AUTHOR, --author or --assignee was stored and echoed verbatim in claim refusals"
  after: "Only a token that provably holds no userinfo is left alone, so scoped-package and blob URLs keep an executable retry; an asserted or configured identity, --assignee, or an identity runtime field carrying URL userinfo is refused with invalid_argument_value, and refusals, warnings and claim envelopes redact a stored one"
  migrate: "Use a plain name for PM_AUTHOR, --author, default_author and --assignee; rewrite a holder stored by an older version with pm update <id> --assignee <name>, or take it over with --force"
escape_class: production_defect
